1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,807
Drop an egg into boiling water, and you've just started a machine you can never switch off.

2
00:00:06,150 --> 00:00:11,784
Inside, the white is full of millions of coiled protein springs, floating free. That's why it pours like liquid.

3
00:00:12,150 --> 00:00:17,513
At sixty-three degrees, the heat shakes those springs until they unravel. And unraveled springs... tangle.

4
00:00:17,899 --> 00:00:23,910
By eighty-two degrees, they've locked into one solid mesh, trapping all the water inside. Liquid becomes rubber.

5
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:30,977
Fry it, you can scrape it. Burn it, you can bin it. But a boiled egg can never be unboiled. The springs never let go.
